tation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"ἀνενεγκεῖν . Lit. to bring or bear up: hence to refer to or bring before a person, to present. The word is used in the Epistle to the Hebrews for \"offer\" as a sacrifice; vii. 27; xiii. 15. [This secondary meaning is brought out in 1 Pet. ii. 24, o$j ἁμαρτίας ἡμων αὐτὸς ἀνήνεγκεν ἐν τῷ σώματι αὐτοῦ ἐπὶ τὸ ξύλον , \"Who bore up our sins in His body upon the cross,\" viz. to expiate them. It is a common word in the LXX. for offering sacrifice, both its primary and secondary meanings corresponding to those of the Hebrew word which it translates.-F. G.]"},{"id":"de4232d3b10b","v":"npnf.chrysostomus.hom_heb","w":"chrysostomus.hom_heb","a":"johannes_chrysostomus","s":28,"p":[21,21],"r":[2,22],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"1 Pet. ii. 22"},{"id":"2c1ee0d2f50d","v":"npnf.basilius.de_spiritu_sancto","w":"basilius.de_spiritu_sancto","a":"basilius_von_casarea","s":7,"p":[1,1],"r":[2,17],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"The word ἀδελφότης is in the New Testament peculiar to S. Peter (1 Peter ii. 17, and v. 9); it occurs in the Epistle of St. Clement to the Corinthians, Chap. ii."},{"id":"b82d5443027b","v":"npnf.basilius.de_spiritu_sancto","w":"basilius.de_spiritu_sancto","a":"basilius_von_casarea","s":15,"p":[2,2],"r":[3,21],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"cf . 1 Pet. iii. 21."},{"id":"9b6951dbc9e1","v":"npnf.basilius.de_spiritu_sancto","w":"basilius.de_spiritu_sancto","a":"basilius_von_casarea","s":15,"p":[3,3],"r":[3,21],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"1 Pet. iii. 21."},{"id":"b037ccbcc60e","v":"npnf.basilius.de_spiritu_sancto","w":"basilius.de_spiritu_sancto","a":"basilius_von_casarea","s":23,"p":[2,2],"r":[1,2],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"cf . Matt. xxviii. 19; 1 Cor. xii. 11; Rom. viii 11; 1 Pet. i. 2."},{"id":"05e4942d3845","v":"npnf.basilius.de_spiritu_sancto","w":"basilius.de_spiritu_sancto","a":"basilius_von_casarea","s":25,"p":[3,3],"r":[1,11],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"1 Peter i. 11."},{"id":"0ff8fb9b28a5","v":"npnf.basilius.de_spiritu_sancto","w":"basilius.de_spiritu_sancto","a":"basilius_von_casarea","s":28,"p":[2,2],"r":[3,21],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"cf . 1 Pet. iii. 21."},{"id":"89bbb9070b90","v":"npnf.basilius.epistulae","w":"basilius.epistulae","a":"basilius_von_casarea","s":22,"p":[1,1],"r":[2,15],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"cf . 2 Cor. xii. 20 and 1 Peter ii. 15."},{"id":"e309a9726419","v":"npnf.basilius.epistulae","w":"basilius.epistulae","a":"basilius_von_casarea","s":22,"p":[1,1],"r":[3,16],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"cf . 1 Peter iii. 16, 17, and James iv. 11."},{"id":"4354d9e0bda4","v":"npnf.basilius.epistulae","w":"basilius.epistulae","a":"basilius_von_casarea","s":22,"p":[1,1],"r":[4,3],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"1 Pet. iv. 3."},{"id":"86c1eb5eb362","v":"npnf.basilius.epistulae","w":"basilius.epistulae","a":"basilius_von_casarea","s":22,"p":[3,3],"r":[2,17],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"Rom xii. 10 and 1 Pet. ii. 17."},{"id":"d6c1b5dce5fc","v":"npnf.basilius.epistulae","w":"basilius.epistulae","a":"basilius_von_casarea","s":42,"p":[3,3],"r":[3,8],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"1 Pet. iii. 8."},{"id":"61aae89e0d99","v":"npnf.basilius.epistulae","w":"basilius.epistulae","a":"basilius_von_casarea","s":161,"p":[2,2],"r":[5,7],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"cf . Ps. lv. 22 and 1 Pet. v. 7."},{"id":"12b52cb764bc","v":"npnf.basilius.epistulae","w":"basilius.epistulae","a":"basilius_von_casarea","s":261,"p":[3,3],"r":[2,22],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"1 Pet. ii. 22."},{"id":"5c7e61623c04","v":"npnf.gregor_nyssa.contra_eunomium","w":"gregor_nyssa.contra_eunomium","a":"gregor_v_nyssa","s":35,"p":[1,1],"r":[3,14],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"mh dexoito . This use of the optative, where the subjunctive with ean might have been expected, is one of the few instances in Gregory's Greek of declension from Classic usage; in the latter, when ei with the optative does denote subjective possibility, it is only when the condition is conceived of as of frequent repetition, e.g. 1 Peter iii. 14. The optative often in this Greek of the fourth century invades the province of the subjunctive."},{"id":"9ff0a2a847af","v":"npnf.gregor_nyssa.contra_eunomium","w":"gregor_nyssa.contra_eunomium","a":"gregor_v_nyssa","s":67,"p":[4,4],"r":[2,8],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"S. 1 Pet. ii. 8."},{"id":"ca920caf304d","v":"npnf.gregor_nyssa.contra_eunomium","w":"gregor_nyssa.contra_eunomium","a":"gregor_v_nyssa","s":83,"p":[1,1],"r":[2,22],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"1 Pet. ii. 22."},{"id":"48dfdcc1002f","v":"npnf.gregor_nyssa.de_virginitate","w":"gregor_nyssa.de_virginitate","a":"gregor_v_nyssa","s":5,"p":[0,0],"r":[1,24],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"1 Pet. i. 24."},{"id":"7eca67baa406","v":"npnf.gregor_nyssa.in_meletium","w":"gregor_nyssa.in_meletium","a":"gregor_v_nyssa","s":1,"p":[0,0],"r":[1,24],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"1 Pet. i. 24; Is. xl. 8."},{"id":"175b2e9d082c","v":"npnf.gregor_nyssa.epistulae","w":"gregor_nyssa.epistulae","a":"gregor_v_nyssa","s":17,"p":[3,3],"r":[2,22],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"1 Pet. ii. 22."},{"id":"af3d2b2557dc","v":"npnf.ambrosius.de_officiis","w":"ambrosius.de_officiis","a":"ambrosius_von_mailand","s":18,"p":[4,4],"r":[3,4],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"1 Pet. iii. 4."},{"id":"f1b3b5d6d86a","v":"npnf.ambrosius.de_officiis","w":"ambrosius.de_officiis","a":"ambrosius_von_mailand","s":21,"p":[4,4],"r":[2,23],"k":"quotation","m":"edi